    title: "AI Overviews",
    abbr: null,
    family: "ai-search",
    badge: "AI Search",
    metaTitle: "What are Google AI Overviews? | Khamare Clarke",
    metaDescription: "Google AI Overviews explained: the AI-generated answer panels at the top of Google search results, and how to appear in them.",
    h1: "AI Overviews: Google's AI-Generated Answers at the Top of Search",
    definition: "Google AI Overviews are AI-generated answer panels that appear at the top of Google search results pages for certain queries, synthesising information from multiple web sources into a concise response with cited links. They are powered by Google's Gemini models and represent the integration of generative AI directly into Google's core search product.",
    whyItMatters: [
      "AI Overviews appear above organic search results, meaning a business cited in an AI Overview receives visibility even above a position-one organic ranking. For the queries where AI Overviews appear (primarily informational and research queries), being in the overview panel is the most prominent position on the page. Not appearing in the overview while competitors do represents a significant visibility gap.",
      "AI Overviews also affect click behaviour. Some users read the overview and do not click through to any source. Others click the cited links to verify or expand on the information. The net effect on organic click-through rates from queries that trigger AI Overviews is a subject of ongoing debate, but what is clear is that appearing as a cited source in the overview is preferable to not appearing at all.",
    ],
    howKhamareApplies: [
      "AI Overview citation is achieved through the same signals that drive broader AEO and GEO visibility: direct, structured answers to specific questions, correct schema markup, entity consistency, and content that Google's systems assess as authoritative on the topic. FAQ pages, definition pages, and content structured around specific questions are the formats most frequently cited in AI Overviews.",
      "Monitoring AI Overview appearances for target queries is part of ongoing AI search tracking. Google Search Console is beginning to surface data on AI Overview impressions and clicks for sites that appear in them. Manual monitoring of target queries in a logged-out browser provides a direct view of whether and how the site is being cited.",
    ],
    faq: [
      { q: "Can I opt out of Google AI Overviews?", a: "Websites can prevent their content from being included in AI Overviews by adding a nosnippet meta tag or by using the max-snippet robots directive to limit the amount of text Google can extract. However, opting out of AI Overviews also typically removes the site from featured snippets and other rich result formats. For most businesses investing in SEO and AI search visibility, opting out of AI Overviews is counterproductive." },
      { q: "Are Google AI Overviews the same as featured snippets?", a: "No. Featured snippets extract a specific passage from a single web page and display it at the top of results. AI Overviews synthesise information from multiple sources into a generated answer. They look different (AI Overviews typically have a more conversational format and cite multiple sources, while featured snippets show a direct passage from one page) and are produced by different mechanisms. A site can appear in featured snippets without appearing in AI Overviews, and vice versa." },
      { q: "What types of queries trigger Google AI Overviews?", a: "AI Overviews appear most frequently for informational and research queries: 'what is X', 'how does Y work', 'best way to Z'. They appear less frequently for transactional queries (where a user is ready to buy) and navigational queries (where a user wants to reach a specific site). This means AI Overview citation is most valuable for building authority and top-of-funnel awareness, while traditional search rankings remain important for capturing bottom-of-funnel commercial intent." },
    ],
    expertisePage: "/expertise/ai-search-optimisation",
    servicePage: "/services/ai-search-optimisation",
